{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And the glory of his forest and his Carmel.</b> A parable, that they were many like the trees of the forest and the Carmel." "<b>From soul to flesh it will consume.</b> That he will obliterate them in the manner of burning." "<b>Like the consuming [כמסוס].</b> A noun like יקוד, and it is not in construct state." "And the meaning of <b>נוסס</b> is that this thing will appear as a banner."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:12.803271780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}